00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:41.250
The morning just after the woods beyond the river had frosted over,

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.570
Mattis came to pick up Birk and Ronja,

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:47.440
and they both went back to the castle.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:51.710
After they returned, those at Mattis' fort and Borka's Keep...

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:57.200
...were overcome with joy such as they had not felt since the unhappy morning they were parted.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:05.170
Duel at Dawn

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:05.170
Duel at Dawn

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.140
I'm so hungry...

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.260
Pelje, let's go!

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.390
Ch-Chief!

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.520
You guys come with us!

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:13.030
Chief...

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.540
They're here!

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.790
Mommy...

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:16.840
And then, when Lil-Klippen saw Pelje's face, he turned pale in surprise,

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:21.800
since he thought that Pelje had been hanged.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.770
He must of thought it was Pelje's ghost talking to him, right?

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.700
On our side, Borka was surprised because...

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:39.610
Mattis had the heart to release the two Borka robbers that had also been captured.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:47.820
But because he released everyone, the sheriff's men were even more upset.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.030
They've started to hunt down robbers.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:09.850
Just few days ago, when I went to the Bear's Cave,

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:13.730
the woods had felt threatening and hostile.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.530
But, it's different now.

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:21.740
Now, the forest gives me nothing but joy.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:31.520
But that's because I know I'm going to be warm right down to my toes when I get back home.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:40.300
If I had to lie shivering in a cold cave afterward,

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.640
I wouldn't be able to think like that.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.580
Yeah, I agree.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:51.190
When I get home from the forest, I head straight for the fireplace in Borka's Keep,

00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:54.130
and curl up like a rabbit.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.220
And you know...

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:04.950
Undis and Borka were so extraordinarily glad when I got home.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:14.620
I would never have imagined that they cared so much about me.

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:19.960
Yeah, you should keep living with them.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.970
Until spring, right?

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:36.350
Pelje!

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:38.510
Hey!

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:47.990
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:51.500
This is just great.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:55.500
That little thief hound can come and go here as he likes.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:59.750
I invited him to come home with us, after all.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:06.840
But if I didn't have to see that red head of his all the time...

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:10.100
...I would at least be able to relax a little.

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:20.030
Here.

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:41.380
No one is going to hang a single one of my robbers!

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:42.460
Yeah!

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:44.150
Of course!

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:45.420
That's right!

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:46.380
Yup!

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:49.300
We are the strongest robbers in this forest!

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:52.250
Yeah! We are the best!

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:58.810
I rescued Pelje from that dungeon, and taught the sheriff a valuable lesson.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.360
What did you teach him?

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:08.290
"Robbers don't sit still, no matter where you put them!"

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:09.490
That's what!

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:10.690
You're right!

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:11.910
That's just like you!

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:13.970
Don't mess with our chief!

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.500
Yahoo!

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.280
The sheriff is nothing compared to us!

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:20.880
I'll follow you forever!

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:23.340
Way to go!

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:25.970
And that's why...

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:32.470
...we've got soldiers swarming through the woods like horseflies.

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:40.020
The sheriff will win in the end, Mattis.

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:44.390
How many times must I tell you?

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:47.280
You and Borka must set aside your differences

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:51.860
and work together as single strong band of robbers.

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:57.790
Only then will you stand a chance against the sheriff and his men.

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:03.880
Two separate bands who cheat each other for loot...

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:08.490
...like wolves vying over morsels of flesh,

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:13.880
or who waste all their time fighting,

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.740
definitely won't win.

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:23.810
You have no idea what you're talking about, old man!

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:27.980
Of course, you <i>are</i> right in a way.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:36.150
But... who do you think would be the chief of that robber band?!

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.770
Borka, eh?

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:48.510
I, Mattis,

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:53.550
am the mightiest robber chieftain in all the mountains and forests!

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:55.250
I'm also the strongest,

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:57.600
and I intend to remain so!

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:02.560
But we can't be so sure that Borka will understand that.

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:08.070
Then you should make him understand.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:15.700
You ought to be able to win a duel against him.

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:20.070
You're like a great ox, after all.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:25.880
Winning the duel would make you the chief of all the robbers,

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:28.630
and bring everyone together.

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:32.260
If we can keep luring the soldiers onto the wrong path...

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:35.640
...or keep them busy chasing their own tails,

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:41.930
they'll eventually get tired of hunting robbers.

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:45.600
What a cunning plan.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:48.400
I...

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:54.320
I think the most cunning idea of all would be to stop robbing.

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:10.630
It's something I've always thought.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:35.700
It's just as Ronja said, Mattis.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:39.450
But I am too old and feeble...

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:45.830
...to drum something like that into your skull.

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:49.000
What about you?!

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:52.670
You were once a bold robber, first under my father, and even under me!

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.720
How can you say such things?!

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:57.470
Stop robbing?!

00:11:57.470 --> 00:12:01.180
What would we live on then?!

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:10.230
Have you ever noticed that there are other people who are not robbers,

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:15.690
and yet they manage to live just fine?

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:17.860
Yeah.

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:21.490
But how?

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:25.040
Of course, there are several ways.

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:28.370
I know of one particularly good way,

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:37.090
but you're not going to quit robbing until you get hung up by your throat, huh?

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:42.750
Even I understand that.

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:48.040
So when the right times comes, I'll talk to Ronja.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:51.310
I'll tell her a nice little secret.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:53.770
Secret?

00:12:56.070 --> 00:12:57.610
Yes, a secret.

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:06.040
I'll tell Ronja so she won't be left helpless on the day you're hanged.

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:09.270
Hanged, hanged, hanged!

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:10.870
Shut up already!

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:13.380
You miserable old croak!

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:36.320
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:36.320
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:41.950
One afternoon, just a few days later...

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:43.760
Mattis!

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:46.370
It's an emergency!

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.680
What is this?! Why did you call me?!

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:06.510
I come with bad news.

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:12.640
Today, no robber who values his life should go into the forest.

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:17.440
Soldiers are waiting in ambush.

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:20.940
Just earlier, one of my robbers was struck by an arrow.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:27.200
But you've come to warn me,

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.950
despite everything that has happened?

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:37.080
It's no trouble, you saved two of my robbers from the sheriff's dungeon, after all.

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:39.760
This is my way of returning the favor.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:48.220
Hey, Borka.

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:54.680
It seems like we will just have to teach these soldiers how to mind their manners.

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:58.470
With our own hands, if it comes down to that.

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:01.440
We...?

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:16.630
What? You're being creepy!

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:27.590
It might be better that we... perhaps... join forces.

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:34.110
For once in your life, Mattis, you've said something quite clever!

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:38.100
One strong band of robbers...

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:39.690
That would be good!

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:49.620
We would need one strong chief to lead such a strong band of robbers.

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:55.120
Mattis, I happen to know a chief who suits that role perfectly.

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:58.250
And that's... me!

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:06.380
I also know somebody who would be the perfect chief.

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:10.890
And that's... me!

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:24.530
Everyone out!

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:38.420
I simply can't stand to listen this ruckus any longer!

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:56.740
I don't want to watch my father fight.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:59.980
Well, you won't be allowed to watch.

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:05.110
"Women and children must keep away from the Wild Beast's Match."

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:09.490
That's how the tradition goes at least.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:14.820
The "Wild Beast's Match" is certainly well named.

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:21.290
It felt like a wild beast's den in here until everyone was kicked out.

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:25.800
It's the same over in Borka's Keep.

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:30.300
My mother was also yelling at them to get out.

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:51.150
I'll batter Borka to bits, until even Undis won't recognize him!

00:17:52.460 --> 00:18:00.660
Brag when you're riding home after the match, that's what my mother always said.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:04.760
But, Skalle-Per,

00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:08.170
you should come with me to the match.

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:12.070
I know you've been feeling poor lately,

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:14.680
but a Wild Beast's Match...

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:18.480
...will put some heart back into you!

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:24.510
Come on, old man.

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:26.790
I'll put you on my horse.

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:30.940
It's about the time to leave, anyway.

00:19:11.740 --> 00:19:14.240
Keep your eyes on me, old man.

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:46.940
Borka! I'm glad you didn't turn your tail and run!

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:52.760
Yeah, I'm also glad you came, Mattis.

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:58.160
I was worried that you would shut yourself up in your fort, afraid to come out.

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:05.490
When you were a child, you would always lock yourself in your room and cry in your bed...

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:10.290
...whenever you were scared!

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:12.000
Shut up!

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:17.550
Instead of wasting time chatting, you should spend it worrying for your life instead!

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:23.350
Ahem.

00:20:24.670 --> 00:20:31.730
Starting now, we'll begin the Wild Beast's Match according to ancestral custom!

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:40.570
In Wild Beast's Matches, every kind of trick or dirty hold is allowed.

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:47.580
Scratching, slapping, tearing, and biting are also allowed!

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:50.090
Break that wild bull's horns!

00:20:50.090 --> 00:20:51.920
Smash him into the pits of hell!

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:53.700
Get him, Mattis!

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:55.590
Beat him like the Borka he is!

00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:57.350
Beat him up, Borka!

00:20:57.350 --> 00:20:59.430
Smash that little weakling Mattis!

00:20:59.430 --> 00:21:01.600
Bite and strike!

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:03.810
However...!

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:09.060
You are allowed to kick, but not between the legs!

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:10.940
Both of you, get ready.

00:21:10.940 --> 00:21:12.650
Get set!

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:20.740
If you want to run away, now is your last chance.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:25.110
Such a thing would only ever happen in your dreams.

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:30.540
But you'll be warm soon, I promise you...

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:33.230
...snot nosed Borka.

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:38.720
And I promise you the same.

00:22:25.430 --> 00:22:29.520
Men are always up to no good.

00:22:41.260 --> 00:22:43.780
Birk, that's the signal to start!

00:22:44.700 --> 00:22:46.990
Well, I wonder how it'll go.

00:23:01.010 --> 00:23:07.610
With that, Mattis and Borka ended up dueling in a Wild Beast's Match,

00:23:07.610 --> 00:23:11.600
just as Skalle-Per had hoped.

